From: dfattal <dfattal@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 22:15:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?inline-3d(#117):=20score=20the=20geometric=20jo?=
 =?UTF-8?q?in=20in=20a=20space=20both=20rects=20can=20occupy=20=E2=80=94?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20the=20top-edge=20raw=20SBS?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ROOT CAUSE of the last standing #117 symptom: "content weaves ok, shows SBS
when leaving from the top less than 50%. No such problem on the bottom."
Reproduced on the model sample, which has no frost, no sticky header and no
child render passes — so neither the frosted-header theory nor the cross-pass
join (withdrawn in 0081) could ever have explained it.

It is an arithmetic defect in one line of the geometric fallback, and both
fingerprints — TOP-only, and a threshold — fall straight out of it.

THE TWO HALVES ARE CLIPPED TO DIFFERENT SPACES, STILL.

A tracked rect is clipped by TransformRectToDestRootTargetSpace (this file,
~line 406) to |dest_root_target_clip_rect| — the EMBEDDING SURFACE's own
root-space footprint, i.e. the web contents area. On a browser window that area
begins BELOW the tab strip and toolbar: every tracked rect in every capture from
the reporting machine is floored at exactly y=218, on two unrelated pages.

|root_output_rect| (browser#94) is the whole WINDOW — "outside root 0,0
2593x1974" in the same logs — starting at y=0.

0080 made best_match clip BOTH rects before taking the ratio, and that was the
right idea; it just clipped them to |root_output_rect|, which the target can
never reach. So for a tile crossing the TOP, the candidate keeps a band 218px
tall that the target cannot have, and that band goes into the denominator:

    score(v) = 1000·v / (v + 218)

for a tile with v pixels still visible. That crosses the 700 bar at v = 509 —
48.8% of the sample's 1043px tile. Below it the tile matches nothing, is
neither suppressed nor woven, and the page draws its raw side-by-side buffer.

The held failing frame is this equation and nothing else:

    target=204,218 1043x481   (46.1% visible)   ->   score 688   vs bar 700

At the BOTTOM edge there is no chrome below the contents, so the surface clip
and the window clip share an edge, the band is zero, and the score is ~1000 at
any visibility. That is the reported "no such problem on the bottom", and it is
why this survived every bottom-edge sweep including 0080's hardware pass.

It also explains the history. Pre-0080 the denominator was the unclipped quad
area and the bar behaved as a ~70%-VISIBILITY gate (the original report). 0080
moved it to ~49% and the symptom shrank rather than disappearing — which is
exactly what the field reports did, from "below ~70%" to "less than 50%".

FIX. Clip to a space both rects can actually occupy. Each Inline3dTrackedRect
now carries the clip it was cut with, and |common_clip_for| cuts the candidate
with the same one (further intersected with |root_output_rect|, so it is never
larger and browser#94's off-viewport reasoning is untouched). Applied at both
scoring sites — the fallback itself and dup_rank. Bottom, sides and the fully
visible case are unaffected: there the clip already agreed, so the score does
not move.

DIAGNOSTIC. The "NO match" line now prints the best REJECTED score and the clip
it was taken in. 688-against-700 and 20-against-700 mean completely different
things, and printing neither is why an arithmetic near-miss read for months as
a mysterious visibility cliff. The next capture confirms or refutes this fix
from that number alone.

STILL OPEN, deliberately not fixed here. The IDENTITY join is dead for this
element at EVERY scroll position — "NO quad anywhere in the frame carries it",
elsewhere=0, on frames that wove correctly as well as frames that did not. The
element's quad IS present and IS correct (above the threshold the fallback
adopts it and the tile weaves right), so this is a STAMPING mismatch, not the
layer being culled: the drawing layer's SharedQuadState does not carry the id
that CollectTrackedElementRects stamped on the rect. That is a real second
defect — it means the whole path runs on a geometric guess — but it is not what
draws raw SBS, and it wants its own investigation with its own hardware gate.
Fixing the arithmetic restores correct weaving at every visibility regardless of
which of the two joins lands the match.

Files:
  components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.{h,cc}

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc | 64 +++++++++++++++++--
 .../viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.h  |  7 ++
 2 files changed, 65 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc b/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc
index 7f67d81..d371abb 100644
--- a/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc
+++ b/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc
@@ -2476,6 +2476,34 @@ AggregatedFrame SurfaceAggregator::Aggregate(
   // buffer. Clipping BOTH rects to the root pass footprint first removes the
   // asymmetry: a 40%-visible tile now scores ~1000 against its own quad, and
   // the bar goes back to meaning "is this the same element".
+  //
+  // browser#117 (TOP-EDGE DEFECT). |root_output_rect| alone is the WRONG common
+  // clip, and it is wrong in one direction only, which is why this reproduced
+  // at the top of the viewport and never at the bottom.
+  //
+  // A tracked rect is clipped by TransformRectToDestRootTargetSpace to the
+  // EMBEDDING SURFACE's root-target clip — the web contents area, which on a
+  // browser window begins below the tab strip and toolbar (y=218 device px on
+  // the reporting machine; every tracked rect in every capture is floored at
+  // exactly that value). |root_output_rect| is the whole WINDOW, from y=0.
+  // Clipping the candidate to the window therefore leaves it holding a band of
+  // height 218 that the target cannot have, and that band inflates the
+  // denominator:
+  //
+  //   score(v) = 1000·v / (v + 218)      for a tile of height H crossing the
+  //                                       TOP with v pixels still visible
+  //
+  // which crosses the 700 bar at v = 509, i.e. 48.8% of a 1043px tile. Below
+  // that the tile matches nothing, is neither suppressed nor woven, and the
+  // page draws its raw side-by-side buffer. The held failing frame is exactly
+  // this: target 204,218 1043x481 (46.1% visible) scores 688. At the BOTTOM
+  // edge there is no chrome below the contents, so both rects are clipped at
+  // the same y, the band is zero and the score is ~1000 at any visibility —
+  // which is precisely the reported "no such problem on the bottom".
+  //
+  // 0080 made this comparison clip-symmetric in NAME; the fix is to clip to a
+  // space both rects can actually occupy. Each tracked rect now carries the
+  // clip it was cut with, and the candidate is cut with the same one.
   auto overlap_score = [](const gfx::Rect& a, const gfx::Rect& b,
                           const gfx::Rect& clip) -> int64_t {
     gfx::Rect ca = a;
@@ -2493,6 +2521,18 @@ AggregatedFrame SurfaceAggregator::Aggregate(
     }
     return (ia * 1000) / max_area;
   };
+  // browser#117: the space BOTH halves of a comparison against |canvas| can
+  // occupy — the root pass footprint further cut by whatever clip that rect was
+  // already cut with. Never larger than |root_output_rect|, so the browser#94
+  // off-viewport reasoning is unaffected.
+  auto common_clip_for =
+      [&root_output_rect](const Inline3dTrackedRect& canvas) {
+        gfx::Rect clip = root_output_rect;
+        if (canvas.root_target_clip) {
+          clip.Intersect(*canvas.root_target_clip);
+        }
+        return clip;
+      };
   auto best_match = [&overlap_score](const gfx::Rect& target,
                                      const std::vector<RootResourceQuad>& quads,
                                      const gfx::Rect& clip)
@@ -2508,6 +2548,7 @@ AggregatedFrame SurfaceAggregator::Aggregate(
     // header. Ties keep the later (topmost) quad, preserving the old behaviour
     // when exactly one candidate qualifies — the slow-scroll/steady case.
     int64_t best_score = -1;
+    int64_t best_rejected = -1;
     for (const RootResourceQuad& cand : quads) {
       // browser#117: candidates recorded for DIAGNOSIS ONLY are not join
       // candidates. This restores the exact pool the recording condition used
@@ -2522,6 +2563,11 @@ AggregatedFrame SurfaceAggregator::Aggregate(
       // browser#117: both rects clipped to |clip| before the ratio, so partial
       // visibility can never read as a mismatch.
       const int64_t score = overlap_score(qr, target, clip);
+      // browser#117: remember the best REJECTED score too. A near-miss (say
+      // 688 against the 700 bar) and a nothing-like-it miss (say 20) mean
+      // completely different things, and the top-edge defect was invisible for
+      // as long as the log printed neither.
+      best_rejected = std::max(best_rejected, score);
       if (score < 700) {
         continue;
       }
@@ -2542,7 +2588,9 @@ AggregatedFrame SurfaceAggregator::Aggregate(
       if ((miss_dbg++ % 60) == 0) {
         VLOG(1) << "[DisplayXR] inline-3D NO match for target="
                 << target.ToString() << " among " << quads.size()
-                << " root quads — overlay left to the page this frame";
+                << " root quads (best rejected score=" << best_rejected
+                << "/1000, bar=700, clip=" << clip.ToString()
+                << ") — overlay left to the page this frame";
       }
     }
     return found;
@@ -2611,7 +2659,7 @@ AggregatedFrame SurfaceAggregator::Aggregate(
         return 0;
       }
       return 1 + std::max<int64_t>(
-                     0, overlap_score(m->rect, r.rect, root_output_rect));
+                     0, overlap_score(m->rect, r.rect, common_clip_for(r)));
     };
     std::vector<Inline3dTrackedRect> deduped;
     deduped.reserve(inline_3d_rects_.size());
@@ -2754,7 +2802,8 @@ AggregatedFrame SurfaceAggregator::Aggregate(
       // browser#117: the fallback compares on the COMMON visible space, so a
       // tile that is only partly on screen scores against its own quad exactly
       // as a fully visible one does.
-      m = best_match(canvas.rect, root_resource_quads_, root_output_rect);
+      m = best_match(canvas.rect, root_resource_quads_,
+                     common_clip_for(canvas));
     }
     if (m) {
       frame.inline_3d_canvas_resources.push_back(
@@ -2946,7 +2995,10 @@ void SurfaceAggregator::CollectTrackedElementRects(
             {TransformRectToDestRootTargetSpace(
                  rect_data.visible_bounds, target_transform,
                  transform_to_root_target, root_target_clip_rect),
-             rect_data.id, rect_data.sqs_layer_id, client_namespace_id});
+             rect_data.id, rect_data.sqs_layer_id, client_namespace_id,
+             // browser#117: keep the clip that was just applied. The join needs
+             // it to compare this rect against an UNCLIPPED quad rect fairly.
+             root_target_clip_rect});
         has_tracked_inline3d = true;
       }
       if (has_tracked_inline3d) {
@@ -2979,8 +3031,8 @@ void SurfaceAggregator::CollectTrackedElementRects(
           {TransformRectToDestRootTargetSpace(rect, target_transform,
                                               transform_to_root_target,
                                               root_target_clip_rect),
-           base::Token(), /*sqs_layer_id=*/0u,
-           std::pair<uint32_t, uint32_t>()});
+           base::Token(), /*sqs_layer_id=*/0u, std::pair<uint32_t, uint32_t>(),
+           root_target_clip_rect});
     }
   }
 }
diff --git a/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.h b/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.h
index 05e2810..e499bb0 100644
--- a/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.h
+++ b/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.h
@@ -492,6 +492,13 @@ class VIZ_SERVICE_EXPORT SurfaceAggregator : public SurfaceObserver {
     base::Token id;
     uint32_t sqs_layer_id = 0;
     std::pair<uint32_t, uint32_t> layer_namespace_id;
+    // browser#117: the root-space clip that TransformRectToDestRootTargetSpace
+    // already applied to |rect| — the embedding surface's own footprint, which
+    // on a browser window starts BELOW the top chrome, not at the window's
+    // y=0. The geometric fallback has to compare in this space or it is not
+    // comparing like with like; see |overlap_score|. Nullopt only when the rect
+    // reached us unclipped.
+    std::optional<gfx::Rect> root_target_clip;
   };
   std::vector<Inline3dTrackedRect> inline_3d_rects_;
 
